# Neo Drive parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoDrive
namespace NeoBuzz.Drive
class NeoDriveMachine
summary Saturator: tape, tube, transistor, diode and wavefolder models with bias, tone filters, auto gain and oversampling. Use it for warmth and grit on tracks, glue on buses, or as a distortion effect.

group Drive
Mode       "Mode"       0 4    0    enum Tape Tube Transistor Diode Fold | Saturation model
Drive      "Drive"      0 1000 250  lin 0 36 dB 1          | Gain into the saturation
Bias       "Bias"       0 1000 500  bip                    | Shifts the curve off centre: even harmonics
Character  "Character"  0 1000 500  pct                    | Tape: emphasis. Tube: sag. Transistor: hardness. Diode: asymmetry. Fold: folds
group Tone
LowCut     "Low cut"    0 1000 0    freq 10 1000           | High-pass before the saturation
Tone       "Tone"       0 1000 500  bip                    | Tilt after the saturation: darker or brighter
HighCut    "High cut"   0 1000 1000 freq 1000 22000        | Low-pass after the saturation
group Output
Output     "Output"     0 1000 500  db -24 24              | Output level
AutoGain   "Auto gain"  0 1    1    switch                 | Holds the level steady as the drive changes
Mix        "Mix"        0 1000 1000 pct                    | Dry/wet (the dry signal is delayed to match)
Quality    "Quality"    0 2    1    enum 2× 4× 8×          | Oversampling
